===Ukraine===
Manager: [[Andriy Shevchenko]]

[[Ukraine national football team|Ukraine]] announced a 35-man preliminary squad on 30 April 2021.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://en.uaf.ua/article/41986 |title=Andriy Shevchenko named the expanded list of players of the national team of Ukraine to participate in the training camp before Euro 2020 |work=[[Ukrainian Association of Football]] |date=30 April 2021 |access-date=1 May 2021 |archive-date=2 June 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210602072617/https://en.uaf.ua/article/41986 |url-status=dead }}</ref> The squad was extended to 36 players on 1 May,<ref>{{cite news |url=https://en.uaf.ua/article/41993 |title=Andriy Shevchenko called Yevhen Konoplyanka to the national team of Ukraine |work=[[Ukrainian Association of Football]] |date=1 May 2021 |access-date=1 May 2021 |archive-date=2 June 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210602072625/https://en.uaf.ua/article/41993 |url-status=dead }}</ref> then reduced to 34 players on 15 May as [[Oleksandr Andriyevskyi]] and [[Volodymyr Shepelyev]] withdrew injured.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://en.uaf.ua/article/42104 |title=The national team of Ukraine gathered in Kharkiv to prepare for Euro 2020 and held the first training session |work=[[Ukrainian Association of Football]] |date=15 May 2021 |access-date=19 May 2021 |archive-date=2 June 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210602072659/https://en.uaf.ua/article/42104 |url-status=dead }}</ref> The squad was further reduced to 33 players on 20 May as [[Vitaliy Buyalskyi]] withdrew injured,<ref>{{cite news |url=https://en.uaf.ua/article/42164 |title=Vitaliy Buyalsky will not help the national team at the Euros |work=[[Ukrainian Association of Football]] |date=20 May 2021 |access-date=23 May 2021 |archive-date=2 June 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210602072642/https://en.uaf.ua/article/42164 |url-status=dead }}</ref> then extended to 34 players on 26 May.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://en.uaf.ua/article/42232 |title=Andriy Shevchenko called up Roman Bezus to the national team of Ukraine |work=[[Ukrainian Association of Football]] |date=26 May 2021 |access-date=26 May 2021 |archive-date=2 June 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210602072640/https://en.uaf.ua/article/42232 |url-status=dead }}</ref> The squad was further reduced to 32 players on 28 May as [[Yevhen Konoplyanka]] and [[Viktor Kovalenko (footballer)|Viktor Kovalenko]] withdrew injured.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://en.uaf.ua/article/42254 |title=News from the camp of the national team of Ukraine: the beginning of the final stage of preparation for Euro 2020 and the final loss of Konoplyanka |work=[[Ukrainian Association of Football]] |date=28 May 2021 |access-date=28 May 2021 |archive-date=2 June 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210602072612/https://en.uaf.ua/article/42254 |url-status=dead }}</ref> The final squad was announced on 1 June.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://en.uaf.ua/article/42294 |title=Officially. Andriy Shevchenko announced the application of the national team of Ukraine for Euro 2020 |work=[[Ukrainian Association of Football]] |date=1 June 2021 |access-date=1 June 2021 |archive-date=2 June 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210602072615/https://en.uaf.ua/article/42294 |url-status=dead }}</ref>

